    "created_at": "2024-02-16T16:10:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-02-16T16:10:20Z",
    "body": "> This is due to [whatwg/html-build#290](https://github.com/whatwg/html-build/issues/290). You have some invalid HTML around that line, but the Rust portion of the build step is fixing it up for you. PR preview doesn't run the Rust portion of the build step, so it fails.\r\n\r\nAhh, thanks. Is there a way to run the local build without the Rust, so it matches what the preview does? Generally I try to make sure things build before I put up a PR, so I was disappointed to see this failure.\r\n\r\n> You can try applying [whatwg/html-build#291](https://github.com/whatwg/html-build/pull/291) locally. Or you can stare really hard at (130197,76) to find the extra end tag.\r\n\r\nThanks. 130197 is a blank line, and I had been staring at 130198 instead. Turns out the problem was on 130196.\r\n",
