    "updated_at": "2024-03-18T21:38:09Z",
    "body": "I can't find a way to unresolve the comment and it's not relevant to this PR anymore since it's been removed, but if Chrome is using HTMLString as a return type it's likely doing nothing more than being a DOMString, or worse case is slower.\r\n\r\nFor context HTMLString comes from Trusted Types and it's an alias for `[StringContext=TrustedHTML] DOMString` which does some enforcement of TT when relevant CSP is set.",
