    "body": "> Sorry for the delay, yeah this is correct, so TLDR if it's a setter or a method param it's a candidate for HTMLString (or ScriptString, and ScriptURLString), otherwise just use the raw type.\r\n\r\nI landed the [change](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/5388595) in Chromium, and it turns out the bindings are smart enough to treat them the same for a return value, just FYI. But now the IDL is at least correct.\r\n\r\n> I've commented on whether we should keep the reflected IDL attributes or not at [#10211 (comment)](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10211#issuecomment-2016364509).\r\n\r\nThanks! Your rationale sounds totally reasonable to me. [Sounds](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10211#issuecomment-2017776461) like @annevk agrees.\r\n\r\n> No need to revert, but [web-platform-tests/wpt@2969dd3](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/commit/2969dd3b1af9126ed769915ff852cb29eb615d52) before this PR merges is somewhat annoying. They should be merged around the same time, ideally by the same person. This PR doesn't even have r+.\r\n\r\nSeems like we're very close to landing this? All comments are resolved.\r\n",
